<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.13.2: Additional Resources</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01483</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.13.2: Additional Resources</md:title>
    <md:uuid>08651344-c0b8-4816-a548-ef093d25c50b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title> Writing Functions from Graphs</title>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTION. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS 0 COMMA 4, 1 COMMA 12, AND 2 COMMA 36.">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_05_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <para>Find the equation of the function graphed above. Then find the value at \(f(5)\).</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
                  <item> Find the value of \(a\), the starting point.</item>
                </list>
             </emphasis> 
            </entry>
            <entry>
        \(a=4\)
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
                  <item> Find the \(b\), the growth factor.</item>
                </list>
             </emphasis> 
            </entry>
            <entry>
        \(b=3\)
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
                  <item> Write the equation of the function.</item>
                </list>
             </emphasis> 
            </entry>
            <entry>
        \(f(x)=4 \cdot 3^x\)
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>
                <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
                  <item> Find \(f(5)\).</item>
                </list>
             </emphasis> 
            </entry>
            <entry>
        \(f(5)=4 \cdot 3^5=972\)
      </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      <title> Try It: Writing Functions from Graphs</title>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Use the graph below to write the equation of the function. Then find \(f(5)\).</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="GRAPH OF AN EXPONENTIAL GROWTH FUNCTION. THE GRAPH PASSES THROUGH THE POINTS 0 COMMA 2, 1 COMMA 8, AND 2 COMMA 32.">
                  <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_05_15_05_02.jpg"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
           </para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the<emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answers:</para>
            <para>Here is how to write the exponential function from the graph:</para>
            <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
              <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
                      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
                        <item> Find the value of \(a\), the starting point.</item>
                      </list>
                   </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
          \(a=2\)
        </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
                      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
                        <item> Find the \(b\), the growth factor.</item>
                      </list>
                   </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
          \(b=4\)
        </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
                      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
                        <item> Write the equation of the function.</item>
                      </list>
                   </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
          \(f(x)=2 \cdot 4^x\)
        </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry>
                   <emphasis>
                      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
                        <item> Find \(f(5)\).</item>
                      </list>
                   </emphasis> 
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
          \(f(x)=2 \cdot 4^5=2048\)
        </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>